#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/combat.adoc:233
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attack value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/game-sequence.adoc:63
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:1
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/siege-and-fortresses.adoc:148
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:10
msgid ""
"The effects of missile weapons are worked out in the Shooting phase. This "
"includes missile fire from troops armed with bows, crossbows and similar "
"weapons as well as long ranged artillery bombardment from weapons such as "
"cannons and stone throwing engines.  All magic attacks also happen in this "
"phase, such as _Balls of Flame_ or _Death Bolts_ hurled by sorcerers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Troops that carry missile weapons such as bows, crossbows and handguns have "
"a separate Attack value.  This is expressed as a number following a slash, "
"thus: 3/1, where 3 is the Attack value in close combat and 1 is the Attack "
"value for shooting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:23
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting-at-a-glance.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Range"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:37
msgid ""
"Most troops have a range of 30cm with their weapons regardless of whether "
"they carry bows, crossbows or whatever. The range represents the tactical "
"area over which the unit operates rather than the literal distance a weapon "
"can shoot and most missile weapons are comparable in this respect. Of "
"course, many artillery pieces can shoot a large boulder, cannon ball or some "
"such missile quite a good distance because their tactical role is to provide "
"long ranged bombardment. In these cases, special rules apply as we shall see "
"later. Various rules for specific weapons are also noted in the Army Lists "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The distance between units is measured stand by stand.  An individual stand "
"must be in range in order to shoot.  This may result in some stands being "
"within range whilst others are out, even though they are in the same unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:44
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting-at-a-glance.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Targets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:50
msgid ""
"Units equipped with missile weapons can shoot once in their turn if they are "
"in range of a [.bo5a]#visible# target.  Units engaged in combat cannot shoot "
"other than to <<shooting-at-charging-enemy,shoot at units that have charged "
"them>>, as described later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:55
msgid ""
"[.qa]#If a unit chooses to shoot, it# automatically shoots at the closest "
"enemy unit it can see. All stands shoot at the same target unit where "
"possible. If two visible enemy units are equally close, the player may "
"choose which to shoot at."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Enemy units in combat are judged to be intermingled with their opponents and "
"don’t therefore present a clear visible target to missile fire. They are "
"consequently ignored as potential targets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:65
msgid ""
"If it’s impossible for every stand to shoot at the same enemy unit then "
"shooting can be divided stand by stand, though this tends to be ineffective."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:85
msgid ""
"In addition to the normal rules for xref:game-values.adoc#line-of-sight[Line "
"of Sight], at least 1cm of the shooting stand should have clear visibility "
"to the target unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:108
msgid ""
"Note that some kinds of terrain affect a unit’s ability to see a target. For "
"example, it is impossible to draw a line of sight through a wood or village "
"– with the exception that stands positioned within 2cm of the edge can see "
"out (and can be seen) and stands inside a wood can see each other up to 2cm "
"away. It is therefore possible for archers to line up at the edge of a wood "
"and shoot out without exposing themselves to a charge from enemy cavalry, [."
"edit]#chariots or monsters# for whom the wood is impenetrable.  See xref:"
"movement.adoc#terrain[Terrain]."
msgstr ""

#.  Caption added
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Targets in and out of sight."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:118
msgid ""
"Some units can see all round – they have 360 degree vision – and you will "
"find this indicated in the unit’s description (for example, Wolf Riders). "
"This means when shooting at the enemy a line of sight can be drawn from any "
"free edge of any stand in the unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculating casualties"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:138
msgid ""
"To work out the effect of missile fire, begin by adding up the unit’s total "
"shooting Attack value. For example, a unit of three stands, each with a "
"shooting Attack value of 1, will have a total value of 3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:144
msgid ""
"The total [.bo5a]#Attack# value is the number of dice rolled to determine "
"how many hits are scored on the target. The minimum dice roll required for a "
"hit is normally 4 or more. So, three dice rolls of 1, 4 and 6 equals two "
"hits on the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:151
msgid ""
"Players may find it convenient to resolve shooting attacks from several "
"units at once if they are firing at the same target. This saves time rolling "
"several batches of dice. Just add up the total number of dice rolls from all "
"the units shooting and roll all the dice at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "Defended or fortified targets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:158
msgid ""
"It is harder to score a hit on a target if it is in a defended or fortified "
"position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:161
msgid ""
"The chart below shows the [.bo5a]#minimum dice roll needed to score a hit on "
"the target#."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO Table consistency
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scores to hit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|[.bo5a]#Target status# |[.bo5a]#Score to hit#\n"
"\n"
"|Infantry or artillery target in a fortified position\n"
"|6\n"
"\n"
"|Infantry or artillery target in a defended position\n"
"|5 or 6\n"
"\n"
"|All other targets\n"
"|4, 5 or 6\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:200
msgid ""
"If some stands in the target unit are defended or fortified whilst others "
"are not, shooters will always target the least protected stands as long as "
"they are able to see them and they are within range, even though other "
"stands may be closer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:206
msgid ""
"If a target unit includes defended or fortified stands as well as stands "
"that are in the open, stands in the open must be removed as casualties first "
"even if they are not the direct targets of the attack (e.g. if they are out "
"of range)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:215
msgid ""
"It can sometimes be necessary to divide the dice rolling into batches as the "
"score required to hit will change once all stands in the open are destroyed. "
"For example, a unit consists of three stands, two defended and one in the "
"open, and is shot at by six enemy stands. It is possible that the first "
"three shots could remove the stand in the open, obliging the remaining three "
"enemy to shoot at a defended target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:225
msgid ""
"If a target unit has armour then the number of hits scored by shooters may "
"be potentially reduced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:230
msgid ""
"The target’s Armour value is expressed as a number 6+, 5+, 4+ or 3+, "
"indicating the minimum dice score required to nullify a hit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:237
msgid ""
"[.bo5a]#The players whose unit has been shot at# rolls one dice for each hit "
"scored on the unit. Any dice that scores equal to or more than the Armour "
"value of the unit will nullify or ‘save’ one hit. Hits nullified in this way "
"are ignored – they are not struck on the target and no further account is "
"taken of them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:244
msgid ""
"For example, a unit of Empire Knights (Armour 4+) is shot at by two units of "
"archers which score four hits. Four dice are rolled for Armour (one dice per "
"hit) scoring 2, 4, 5 and 6.  As any score of 4 or more equals a ‘save’, 3 "
"hits are nullified and the Knights suffer only one hit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:246
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removing casualties"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:253
msgid ""
"Units can sustain a number of hits before a stand is destroyed and this "
"number varies depending upon how tough and how determined the target is. Men "
"have a value of 3, for example, whilst dour, stubborn-minded Dwarfs have a "
"value of 4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:258
msgid ""
"Once a unit has taken a number of hits equal to its Hits value, [.bo5a]#its "
"player# removes a stand.  [.bo5a]#Always take a stand from the edge of the "
"formation, never the middle, so the unit retains and viable formation.#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:265
msgid ""
"If the unit takes insufficient hits to destroy a stand, or if it suffers "
"enough to remove a stand with some remaining, record any hits left over. "
"This is most easily done by placing a distinctively coloured dice directly "
"behind the unit so that it shows the number of hits the unit has taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:270
msgid ""
"If a unit is shot at by several enemies during the Shooting phase it may "
"take further hits and the total may mount up. Remove stands as casualties "
"occur and record any hits left over as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:279
msgid ""
"Once the Shooting phase is over, any odd hits are discounted. Hits are not "
"recorded from one phase to another or from one turn to the next.  We assume "
"that the regiment regroups while lightly wounded or disaffected warriors are "
"brought back into the fighting ranks. Although this means that it is quite "
"difficult to inflict casualties by shooting, missile fire can be used to "
"drive back enemy units, as follows."
msgstr ""

#.  Difference: Bo5A allows changing formation.
#.  Caption added.
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:283
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:341
#, no-wrap
msgid "Driving back enemies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:291
msgid ""
"At the end of the Shooting phase, units that have taken hits during the "
"phase are driven back by the hail of missiles. This can be thought of as an "
"orderly retreat under fire or as an out-and-out flight followed by a swift "
"rally, depending on the distance involved. The more hits a unit suffers, the "
"further it is likely to be driven back."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:297
msgid ""
"Work out how far units are driven back once all shooting is complete but "
"*before* disregarding odd hits at the end of the Shooting phase. The player "
"whose units are being driven back can decide the order in which drive backs "
"are resolved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:305
msgid ""
"To determine how far units are driven back, the opposing player rolls one "
"dice for each hit suffered. Don’t forget to include hits from any stands "
"that have been removed during the phase. Add up the total of all the dice to "
"find how far the unit is driven back. For example, a unit taking two hits "
"rolls two dice scoring 3 and 4, resulting in the unit being driven back 7cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:310
msgid ""
"A unit that has one or more stands in a defended position disregards the "
"first hit suffered when working out drive backs. This means one hit cannot "
"cause a drive back, two hits roll one dice, three hits roll two dice and so "
"on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:316
msgid ""
"A unit that has 1 or more stands in a fortified position disregards the "
"first two hits suffered when working out drive backs. This means one or two "
"hits cannot cause a drive back, three hits roll 1 dice, four hits roll 2 "
"dice and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:324
msgid ""
"Units that are driven back move directly away from the closest enemy stand "
"that shot at them regardless of whether that enemy inflicted any hits – this "
"is called the driving unit. Driving units will normally be units of troops, "
"but can also be enemy wizards if the unit has been affected by an "
"appropriate spell (such as _Ball of Flame_)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:337
msgid ""
"When a unit is driven back, it is moved directly away from the enemy without "
"changing its formation or orientation. The direction of the drive back is "
"established by placing a ruler or other straight edge between the closest "
"enemy stand and the closest part of the unit as shown in the diagram above. "
"This is similar to an evade move as described in the xref::movement.adoc#the-"
"path-of-evaders[Movement section], but note that in the case of an evade, "
"the unit can change its formation and stands can change their orientation as "
"they move, in the case of a drive back, a unit can do neither of these "
"things but must move back as a block. See <<drive-back>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:345
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units confused during drive backs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:351
msgid ""
"Units that have been driven back may become confused amidst the turmoil of a "
"disorderly recoil. This is a marked disadvantage because it means that units "
"will be unable to move in their following [.bo5a]#Command phase#."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:354
msgid ""
"When rolling for drive back distances, any dice roll of a 6 means that the "
"unit becomes *confused*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:359
msgid ""
"Units may also become confused if they are driven back into terrain which "
"they can’t enter or if they are driven back into other units, whether they "
"are friend or foe. See the section on xref::confusion.adoc[Confusion] for "
"full rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:361
#, no-wrap
msgid "Units routed by drive backs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:368
msgid ""
"If the Drive back dice roll is greater than the unit’s full pace movement "
"distance, then the unit is automatically deemed to have fled from the battle "
"in rout. The unit is not moved – instead the entire unit is removed as a "
"casualty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:373
msgid ""
"This happens rarely because units taking many hits are usually destroyed as "
"a result. Large monsters with many hits are more likely to be destroyed in "
"this fashion than infantry or cavalry units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:377
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shooting at charging enemy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:386
msgid ""
"Stands capable of shooting (including artillery, appropriate monsters and "
"some machines) can shoot at enemy units charging their own unit.  These "
"shots represent the unit pelting the enemy with missiles as they approach, "
"perhaps at the very last moment but possibly as part of a fighting "
"withdrawal by parties posted ahead of the unit’s main body."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:390
msgid ""
"Shooting in this way is an exception to the normal turn sequence because it "
"happens in the [.bo5a]#Command phase of the# enemy’s turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:395
msgid ""
"Remember, a unit is ‘charged’ so long as it is contacted by a charging stand "
"– it does not matter if the unit was not the original target of the charge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:407
msgid ""
"A stand can shoot at charging enemy even if its own unit is already engaged "
"in combat. In this case, only stands that are not already touching an enemy "
"can shoot. Stands that are already touching an enemy cannot shoot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:419
msgid ""
"Shots are worked out as soon as the charging unit has finished its move. "
"Shooting stands must be able to draw a line of sight to the enemy unit at "
"some point during the charge move whilst it is within their weapon range. "
"This can be at any moment during the charge: either at the start of the "
"move, once it is complete or at any point in between.  Note that some troops "
"are allowed to shoot all round (e.g., Wolf Riders) and they can therefore "
"shoot by drawing a line of sight from any edge – other troops must draw a "
"line of sight from their front edge as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:425
msgid ""
"Calculate the effect of shots and remove any whole stand casualties straight "
"away before moving any further units.  Because casualties are removed at "
"once, this can potentially create a line of sight for another unit to charge "
"into a space vacated by the casualty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:432
msgid ""
"Note that shots from bolt throwers can penetrate enemy stands and affect "
"other stands or units behind the target.  Shots are always calculated from "
"the position of the chargers at the beginning or at the end of their move – "
"so penetration can be easily calculated from the starting or the final "
"position of the charging unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:443
msgid ""
"Hits inflicted on the charging enemy unit are carried over into the combat. "
"When it comes to working out combat results, these hits count as having been "
"struck in the first combat round. If enough shooting hits are caused to "
"destroy one or more charging stands, then casualties are removed immediately "
"and do not therefore fight in the Combat phase. Remember – the total number "
"of shooting hits count as having been struck in the first combat round even "
"where whole stands have been removed, as shown in diagrams <<shooting-at-"
"chargers>> and <<shooting-hits-carried-over>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:451
msgid ""
"_For example, if an Archer unit inflicts two hits on a unit of charging "
"Knights, the Knights start the combat with two hits outstanding and these "
"will count towards the combat result for the first round. If three hits were "
"inflicted, then one stand is removed and will not fight in the combat – the "
"three hits still count as having been struck in the first combat round._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:459
msgid ""
"Hits on charging units don’t cause drive backs. This is partly for "
"convenience, as the game would quickly become very cluttered otherwise, but "
"it also reflects the ability of troops to stoically advance under fire once "
"they have the enemy in sight. Any loss of enthusiasm is taken into account "
"by including any hits inflicted in the result for the first round of "
"fighting (see xref::combat.adoc#combat-results[Combat results]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:460
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Archers shoot as the Knights charge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:470
msgid ""
"If a missile-armed unit is charged by two or more enemy units, one after the "
"other, then it can potentially shoot more than once. When shooting at a "
"second or subsequent charger only those stands that are not already engaged "
"can fire. Remember that stands touching corner-to-corner are engaged and so "
"are not free to shoot at charging enemy."
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: Low-priority diagram.
#.  2 changed to Two to avoid adjacent figure number.
#. type: Block title
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:473
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two hits are scored – not enough to remove a stand – but these hits are carried over into the first combat round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:479
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/siege-and-fortresses.adoc:1665
#, no-wrap
msgid "Special situations"
msgstr ""

#.  Edit grammar
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:489
msgid ""
"When a unit hit by shooting or magic is engaged in combat, or becomes "
"engaged in combat by the end of shooting phase, it cannot be driven back. "
"Any hits scored count as having been struck in the first round of combat "
"that turn. Note that this will only occur in some very special situations "
"mostly due to magic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:493
#, no-wrap
msgid "The role of missile troops"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:502
msgid ""
"You may have realised by now that missile fire isn’t a terribly effective "
"way of destroying enemy units. The number of hits inflicted will probably be "
"insufficient to remove a stand and any odd hits are always discounted at the "
"end of the phase. The most effective way to employ missile fire is to "
"coordinate attacks from several units at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/rules/pages/shooting.adoc:509
msgid ""
"However, shooting is a very effective way of pinning down enemy troops and "
"driving them from strongly defended positions. Good generals will recognise "
"these qualities immediately, for they are an important means of controlling "
"the battlefield and frustrating your enemy’s plans."
msgstr ""
